    <item>
      <title>CA 6. Laplace</title>
      <link>https://buezw.github.io/docs/uoft/26w/ece221---circuit-analysis/ca6.laplace/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 18 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <author>youremail@example.com (Buezwqwg)</author>
      <guid>https://buezw.github.io/docs/uoft/26w/ece221---circuit-analysis/ca6.laplace/</guid>
      <description>&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Last Edit: 3/18/26&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the previous cases, we used transfer from Time Domain to Phasor Domains to analyze circuit with &lt;strong&gt;Sinusoidal Steady-State&lt;/strong&gt;, but we suggest this method is too limited. To use Laplace Transform, we are able to deal with more general ones&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
