    <item>
      <title>CA 3. RLCCircuit</title>
      <link>https://buezw.github.io/docs/uoft/26w/ece221---circuit-analysis/ca3.rlccircuit/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 09 Feb 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <author>youremail@example.com (Buezwqwg)</author>
      <guid>https://buezw.github.io/docs/uoft/26w/ece221---circuit-analysis/ca3.rlccircuit/</guid>
      <description>&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Last Edit: 2/9/26&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;


&lt;h1 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Linear Ordinary Differential Equation, ODE 
    &lt;div id=&#34;linear-ordinary-differential-equation-ode&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
    
    &lt;span
        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 ltr:-left-6 rtl:-right-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;
        &lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34;
            style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#linear-ordinary-differential-equation-ode&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;        
    
&lt;/h1&gt;
$$
a_n x^{(n)} + a_{n-1} x^{(n-1)} + \dots + a_1 x^{(1)} + a_0 x = g(t)
$$&lt;p&gt;$x^{(n)}$: x’s n th derivative for t&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
